<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khmelnytsky Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1648">1648</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khmelnytsky Uprising was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> rebellion that began in 1648 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> in the Ukrainian lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. Drawing on Cossack, peasant and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> grievances against Polish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a>, it inflicted heavy defeats on Commonwealth forces. The revolt led eventually to Russian involvement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and opened a period of wars that severely weakened the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khmelnytsky-uprising.jpg" alt="Khmelnytsky Uprising" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mykola Ivasiuk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pic_I_V_Ivasiuk_Mykola_Bohdan_Khmelnytskys_Entry_to_Kyiv.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
